RT 2 TERMS APPLICABLE TO OFFERED SERVICES 20.&nbsp;&nbsp;GENERALLY In addition to the general conditions set out in these Terms of Use, this Section contains additional terms and conditions that relate to particular Offered Services. Enbridge reserves the right to withdraw any of the following Offered Services at any time upon reasonable notice, which notice may be provided through this Website, or in such other manner as Enbridge determines appropriate in the circumstances. 21. ELECTRONIC BILLING SERVICES By enrolling for electronic billing services (the \"e-Billing Services\"), you will no longer receive a paper bill. You will receive an email to notify you when your electronic bill is ready for viewing. It is your responsibility to ensure that your information including email address is correct and up to date. Failure to receive email notification does not limit your obligation to pay your bill on time. Once enrolled and for so long as you are using the e-Billing services, you have a limited, personal, non-transferable license to view, download an electronic version and print your bill and any inserts or enclosures (collectively the \"Materials\"). You may not alter, change, distort or otherwise modify the Materials or any content contained therein, including the amount and description of the charges on the bill or any terms or any proprietary notices contained on any of the Materials. You will not access or attempt to access any Materials, including the bill, of any other person. Printed copies of your electronic bill cannot be used to pay at a bank or by mailing a cheque. The Exclusion and Limitation of Liability contained within Section 10 of the Terms of Use shall extend to and apply to the benefit of any third parties whose charges appear on the electronic bill or who have contributed enclosures or inserts to the electronic bill. The e-Billing Services are governed by the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein, excluding the co